    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nFiles\n\n### Description\n\nHello o/\r\n\r\nWhen dealing with medium-sized projects, it's common for files to have nested extensions, like the following:\r\n```\r\nfoo.hxx\r\nfoo.ixx\r\nfoo.txx\r\nfoo.cxx\r\nfoo.test.cxx\r\nfoo.test.testscript\r\n```\r\n\r\nNesting is typically managed through a tree, resulting in the following structure:\r\n\r\n```\r\n.\r\n├── foo.cxx\r\n│   ├── foo.hxx\r\n│   ├── foo.ixx\r\n│   ├── foo.txx\r\n│   └── foo.test.cxx\r\n│       └── foo.test.testscript\r\n```\r\n\r\nFor mini.files, where we use a Miller column approach, we could consider introducing a new column specifically for nested files:\r\n\r\n```\r\n.\r\n| foo.cxx | foo.hxx      > | foo.test.testscript\r\n│ ...     | foo.ixx      ^\r\n│ ...     | foo.txx      ^\r\n│ ...     | foo.test.cxx ^\r\n│         \r\n```\r\n\r\nLet me know what you think. ☕️\r\n\r\nRef:\r\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/visualstudio/ide/file-nesting-solution-explorer?view=vs-2022\r\nhttps://www.jetbrains.com/help/rider/File_Nesting_Dialog.html\r\nhttps://code.visualstudio.com/updates/v1_67#_explorer-file-nesting\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
